  "metadata": {
    "title": "Tesla upgraded, Lululemon downgraded: Wall Street's top analyst calls",
    "byline": null,
    "published_at": null,
    "site_name": "finance.yahoo.com",
    "language": null
  },
  "content": {
    "text": "The most talked about and market moving research calls around Wall Street are now in one place. Here are today's research calls that investors need to know, as compiled by The Fly.\nTop 5 Upgrades:\n-\nJPMorgan upgraded Tesla (TSLA) to Neutral from Underweight with a price target of $475, up from $145. The firm says Tesla is at the \"forefront of physical AI\" and entering \"uncharted\" total addressable markets. Erste Group also upgraded Tesla to Hold from Sell.\n-\nErste Group upgraded Broadcom (AVGO) to Buy from Hold. Broadcom is growing much faster than its peers in the sector and the stock should continue its upward trend as it benefits from the company's above-average prospects, the firm tells investors.\n-\nJPMorgan upgraded Chipotle (CMG) to Overweight from Neutral with a price target of $35, down from $38, after meeting with management. At or below $30 per share, JPMorgan sees \"much more risk-weighted upside than downside.\"\n-\nEvercore ISI upgraded FormFactor (FORM) to Outperform from In Line with a $155 price target. The firm thinks a higher multiple is justified given the AI tailwinds and likes the risk/reward at current levels.\n-\nBernstein upgraded Kanzhun (BZ) to Outperform from Market Perform with a price target of $18, up from $16.50. The firm believes high-frequency data has continued to look supportive of Kanzhun's billings growth.\nTop 5 Downgrades:\n-\nBNP Paribas downgraded Lululemon (LULU) to Underperform from Neutral with an $88 price target. Fundamentals come back into focus after last night's Q1 results and \"disappointing\" guidance, the firm tells investors. BTIG also downgraded Lululemon but to Neutral from Buy with no price target following the company's Q1 report and guidance.\n-\nErste Group downgraded Walmart (WMT) to Hold from Buy. Shares are highly valued in relation to the expected earnings growth and in comparison, to competitors, which limits further upside potential, the firm tells investors.\n-\nBerenberg downgraded CrowdStrike (CRWD) to Hold from Buy with a price target of $720, up from $525. The firm cites valuation for the downgrade following the \"solid\" fiscal Q1 report.\n-\nErste Group downgraded Cboe Global Markets (CBOE) to Hold from Buy. The firm expects the company's growth momentum to slow in the coming quarters given the \"significant fall\" in equity and bond market volatility.\n-\nErste Group downgraded CME Group (CME) to Hold from Buy. The firm says that when geopolitical uncertainties subside, trading volumes and transaction fees may fall again and as such, it expects CME's positive revenue momentum to date to weaken over the course of the year.",
